WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.290
- Thanks to Mack Weldon for
keeping Legal Eagle in the air,

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.530
and helping me look fly.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.940
Well, because this is
clearly the darkest timeline,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.470
many have asked, and now I
must answer the question,

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.545
what if the president refuses
to leave the White House?

00:00:14.545 --> 00:00:18.045
(dramatic music)

00:00:18.045 --> 00:00:19.970
(sirens wail)

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.226
- You'll never take me alive, coppers!

00:00:22.226 --> 00:00:23.821
- Get him!
(sirens wail)

00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:25.974
(gunshots blast)
(sirens wail)

00:00:25.974 --> 00:00:28.807
(dramatic music)

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.130
- Hey, Legal Eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.980
and the Secret Service.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.610
As I discussed in a recent video,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.170
Joe Biden is now the clear
winner of the 2020 election,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.170
and Donald Trump's lawsuits
are not going to be enough

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.730
to change that result.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.350
After it looked obvious
that President Trump

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.240
could not get enough
votes to be reelected,

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.270
the media started asking
whether President Trump

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.810
would make a concession speech.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.520
President Trump did not win enough votes

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.760
to win the election, but
he has so far refused

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.350
to concede his loss.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.330
And although no president has
ever refused to leave office,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.330
other elected officials in
the US have thrown tantrums

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.920
after losing an election.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.310
In 1874, Texas Governor
Edmund Davis locked himself

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.200
in the basement of the
state capitol building

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.050
after losing to Richard Coke.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.370
Like Trump, Davis claimed that

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.760
there had been voter fraud,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.970
and the state supreme court,

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.230
with three judges appointed
by Davis, ruled in his favor,

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.290
but Coke was still inaugurated.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.020
Coke then arrived at the state capitol

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.660
with the sheriff's posse.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.840
But Davis appealed to fellow Republican,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.200
President Ulysses S.
Grant, for federal troops,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.500
but Grant refused.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.750
Davis left three days later.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.150
In 1946, there was a standoff in Georgia

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.630
known as the three governors crisis.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.260
After the governor elect
died before taking office,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.670
the outgoing governor thought
he had a right to stay.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.190
The son of the governor elect thought

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:44.540
he should inherit the office,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.280
and the lieutenant governor elect believed

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.580
that he was now governor.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.840
Bizarrely, the state
assembly voted for the son

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.210
to inherit the office.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.660
The two other men were
still in the building,

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.330
but that crisis ended when
the governor elect's son

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.770
changed the locks.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.130
But if that happens this year,

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:01.370
I'll finally get to collaborate
with the LockPickingLawyer.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.530
Now, President Trump hasn't
locked himself in the bathroom

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.700
yet, but he is refusing
to concede that he lost.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.380
Normally, the loser would have given

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.650
a public concession speech by now.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:10.790
That's what Jimmy Carter did

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.740
when Ronald Reagan defeated him in 1980,

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.360
and what George H.W. Bush did in 1992,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.840
when he lost his reelection
bid to Bill Clinton.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.340
But what is a concession speech?

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.400
Well, it's a public
acknowledgement by the loser

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.940
of the presidential race that he or she

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.510
has lost the election.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.880
This is not a legal requirement,

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.820
but it is an important norm that ensures

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.390
the peaceful transfer of power,

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.720
especially since the
incumbent commands, you know,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.730
the whole military until the
next president takes office.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.170
The concession speech generally allows

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.210
the rest of the steps required to confirm

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.000
the election results to move forward.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.040
After the loser concedes,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.070
lots of things happen behind-the-scenes.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.540
This triggers the release of
millions of federal dollars

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.000
to the transition team, along
with access to office space,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.540
and necessary equipment,
like computers and money.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.100
Under the 2015 Presidential
Transitions Improvement Act,

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.210
which amended the 1963
Presidential Transition Act,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.600
the president must establish

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.120
a White House coordinating committee,

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.530
and council of agency transition directors

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.580
six months prior to the election.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.730
Typically, the administrator

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.400
of the General Services
Administration, or GSA,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.680
signs a letter when the winner of the race

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.390
is, quote, "apparent."

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.050
This acts as the federal
government's formal declaration

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.270
that the presidential race is
over and a winner has emerged.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.270
Although every agency including the GSA

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.997
has detailed transition
plans as required by law,

00:03:22.997 --> 00:03:24.930
"The Washington Post" has reported that

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.960
the plans won't move
forward until a winner

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.870
is declared by the GSA.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.670
This could mean a number
of different things,

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.370
that the transition won't
happen until Trump gives up,

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.740
or that everyone is waiting
for the Supreme Court

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.410
to declare a winner.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.770
But that's kind of not how this happens.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.240
In its guidance in April
on how agencies should be

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.090
preparing, the Office of
Management and Budget noted

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.290
that the committee would meet on May 27th.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.460
However, the GSA refused to publish

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.880
the full minutes of this meeting.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.730
We now know that Emily Murphy,

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.580
the President
Trump-appointed administrator

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.030
of the General Services Administration,

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.460
is refusing to sign a letter that

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.480
immediately allows the transfer of power

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.680
from one administration to the next.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.530
When "The Washington Post" asked her why,

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.957
her spokesperson said, quote,

00:04:04.957 --> 00:04:06.817
"An ascertainment has not yet been made,

00:04:06.817 --> 00:04:09.397
"and its administrator
will continue to abide by,

00:04:09.397 --> 00:04:12.400
"and fulfill all
requirements under the law."

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.520
What these two facts, the OMB censoring

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.870
the transition meeting notes,

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.010
and Murphy refusing to
acknowledge the reality

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.880
of President Trump's loss,
what do those tell us?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.850
At a minimum, the Trump team
has no intention of cooperating

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.750
with the peaceful transition of power,

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.150
and both President Trump
and members of his cabinet

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.260
have hinted that they
are not going to comply

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.010
with a peaceful transition,

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.940
with in particular Mike
Pompeo, the Secretary of State,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.820
saying that-

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.940
- There will be a smooth transition

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.690
to a second Trump administration.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.480
- But the stakes of a delayed transition

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.540
are actually higher than one might think.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.410
The bipartisan 9/11 Commission found that

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.970
the delayed transition in 2000

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.980
between the Clinton and
Bush administrations

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.110
actually made the 9/11
attacks more likely,

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.190
because it hampered the
incoming W. Bush administration

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.380
from focusing on the looming
Al-Qaeda threat from day one.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.890
The delayed transition in
2020 might undermine efforts

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.210
to distribute a COVID-19 vaccine.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.030
As the US hits an all time high

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.840
for positive coronavirus tests,

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.120
the Trump COVID task
force has stopped meeting,

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.070
and its chair, Mike Pence,
is trying to go on vacation.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.900
But on top of screwing up the transition,

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.010
there's all kinds of stuff that

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.690
a nefarious squatting president
could do on the way out.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.990
This probably deserves its own video,

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:22.410
but those steps could
include firing not only

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.380
political appointees who
the president doesn't like,

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.230
but also career staff to
just gum up the works.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:29.640
We've seen that already
by President Trump firing

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.080
Defense Secretary Mark Esper,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.720
and the potential firings
of FBI Director Chris Wray,

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.180
and CIA Director Gina Haspel.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.840
The president has also named Michael Ellis

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.260
as NSA General Counsel
in these waning months,

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.500
and you'll remember that name
if you've watched my video

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.760
on how the White House conducted

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.500
a political motivated review
of John Bolton's book.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.250
Ellis was the political operative,

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.410
who took a hatchet to it,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.420
and prevented it from being published.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.250
These could be chaos moves,
or attempts to install

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.960
true believers to take affirmative action

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.490
benefiting President Trump.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.160
The president could pardon
everyone in his orbit,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.890
including his family, his
friends, his co-conspirators,

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:06.100
and maybe even himself,

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.760
and that's not even with respect

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.130
to underlying investigations themselves.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.840
As national security analyst
Asha Rangappa points out,

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.470
the Trump DOJ could induce
the Office of Legal Counsel

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.190
to adopt all kinds of formal positions

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.840
to justify the president's prior acts.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.260
And to the extent there are
actually open investigations

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.510
into President Trump
personally and his family,

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.980
the Department of Justice
could paper over these files,

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:30.260
adding memos that justify
closing of the cases,

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.840
or saying that the
cases were never brought

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.330
in good faith in the first place,

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.780
and calling into doubt the evidence

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:37.520
that's in those investigatory files.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.490
And then, of course, there
are the files themselves.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.520
While destroying records
that have administrative,

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.860
historical, informational,
or evidentiary value

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.920
under the Presidential Records
Act is usually illegal,

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.630
it's probably a good
idea to keep an eye out

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.830
for gray smoke coming out
of the White House chimneys

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.420
in the coming days.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.840
But all of that is during
the transitional period.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.090
What if Donald Trump remains
in denial about the election,

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.750
and continues barking
orders at the military,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.410
and holds onto the football?

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.710
Well, Joe Biden is scheduled
to be sworn in as president

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:08.830
at noon on January 20th, 2021.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:11.670
So as of that date, what
happens if President Trump

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.810
is still throwing a
tantrum, and won't leave?

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:17.190
What if he is a trespasser
on the White House grounds?

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.290
Well, let's start with the Secret Service.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.430
The president loses all
constitutional authority

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:24.550
when his term ends on January 20th, 2021.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:27.060
At this time, he no longer
commands the armed forces,

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.340
or the Secret Service.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.680
Both of those entities will
be commanded by Joe Biden.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.550
When President Biden
arrives at the White House

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:36.520
after his inauguration, he'll
be accompanied by moving vans

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.670
and the US Secret Service.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.620
The Secret Service is a
law enforcement agency

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.880
within the Department
of Homeland Security.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.860
The Secret Service has two roles.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.210
They investigate counterfeiting
and other federal crimes,

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.530
and they protect national
leaders and their families,

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.500
as well as foreign dignitaries.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.480
But what happens if a
president the Secret Service

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.790
has sworn to protect decides
that he's still president,

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.580
and won't leave the White House grounds?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.080
Under the Former Presidents Act,

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.190
the Secret Service provides
lifetime protection

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:03.250
to former presidents and their families.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.610
President Trump will be assigned

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.640
a Secret Service protection
unit that takes over

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.480
after he is no longer president.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.870
But that doesn't mean that President Trump

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.380
has legal authority over
his post-presidential team.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.640
The Secret Service is led by a director.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.510
The current director is James Murray.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.760
The director is appointed by,

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.650
and serves at the
pleasure of the president,

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:23.050
and is not subject to Senate confirmation.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.400
When Biden becomes president,

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.450
Murray reports to Biden, and not Trump.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:27.450
If it came down to a battle

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.460
between President Biden's protective team

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.060
versus Trump's protective team,

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.580
well, it won't, because President Biden

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.210
and Director Murray would order

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.090
former President Trump's
security detail to stand down.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.060
But could some members
of the Secret Service

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.840
decide to disobey Biden's
orders, and fight for Trump?

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:44.870
I mean, theoretically,

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.290
but they'd be committing a felony.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.760
Section 3056 d of Title
18 prohibits knowingly

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.700
and willfully obstructing, resisting,

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.470
or interfering with a federal
law enforcement agent,

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.940
who is engaged protective functions.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:59.010
And if former President
Trump's security detail

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.210
was prosecuted under 18 USC 3056,

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:04.080
it's not even necessary
to show that Trump's guys

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.330
used force against federal
law enforcement agents.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.610
Even blocking the entry to
the White House grounds,

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.180
or the White House doors is considered

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.110
obstruction or resistance.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.770
And of course, the law does
authorize Secret Service agents

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.550
to arrest anyone engaging in activity,

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.560
which could nullify, or
reduce the effectiveness

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.660
of security precautions
taken by the Secret Service.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.200
That means if former President
Trump's Secret Service team

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.750
locks the doors to the
Oval Office or bathroom,

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:27.630
they could be arrested,

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.080
and the government
doesn't even need to prove

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.800
that this interference was
forcible, or aggressive.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.070
It's also a felony under 18 USC 111

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.060
to forcibly assault, resist,
oppose, impede, intimidate,

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.600
or interfere with federal
law enforcement officers,

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.400
including Secret Service agents,

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.030
in the performance of their duties.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.270
People who work for Secret Service

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.980
are well-versed in these laws,

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.160
and many of them have served for decades.

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.350
It's highly unlikely that
large numbers of them

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.453
would turn the White House into the Alamo.

00:09:53.453 --> 00:09:54.286
(gunshot blasts)

00:09:54.286 --> 00:09:56.270
And there are also other
Secret Service support units

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.680
that could be called on to help oust

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.960
a squatting former President Trump.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.860
The Secret Service's uniformed division

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.560
protects facilities and venues secured

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.430
for US Secret Service protectees,

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:06.810
including the White House complex,

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.990
and the vice president's residence
at the Naval Observatory.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.630
These are probably the
people who'd be called on

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.530
to repel any threats to the White House,

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:15.380
or the vice president's residence.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.330
So if President Trump asked the Proud Boys

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.050
to no longer stand by,
but to actually engage,

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.780
these are probably the people
that would act immediately.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.850
And the Secret Service also
has some specialized units,

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.150
which could be called upon to
remove Trump and his allies.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.160
The Emergency Response Team provides

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.210
a coordinated tactical
response for the White House

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.780
and other protected facilities.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.130
The Counter Sniper Team uses observation,

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.130
sighting equipment, and
high-performance weapons

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.030
to provide a secure
environment for protectees.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.690
And if a Trump militia were on the scene,

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.090
those special units would
coordinate a response.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.180
And then there's also the
Motorcade Support Unit,

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:50.910
providing motorcycle tactical support

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:52.940
for official movements of motorcades.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.080
So President Biden
would be safely escorted

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.320
to the White House premises,

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.830
even if an army of
lifted Ford F-250 trucks

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:02.320
with giant, oversized flags showed up

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.590
to block President Biden's advance.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.820
And frankly, I wouldn't mess
around with the Secret Service.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.830
They have plenty of
firepower to back it up.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.860
Agents and officers use
the FN P90 submachine gun,

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.420
the nine millimeter H&amp;K MP5,

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:18.420
a 12-gauge Remington shotgun,
and 5.56 SR-16 QCB rifle.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.670
They also have plenty of
non-lethal options as well,

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:25.070
like a 16-inch expandable
baton, and also pepper spray.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:28.180
Now, to be clear, none of
this is going to happen.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.670
The worst case scenario
is that a President Biden

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:33.800
would simply kindly ask former
President Trump to leave,

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.650
and I'm sure that
President Trump will have

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:38.330
plenty to do and plenty of places to go

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.680
when his term expires.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.800
But if push came to shove,

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.950
the Secret Service would be capable

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.780
of perp walking former
President Trump out,

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:49.360
and dumping him onto Pennsylvania Avenue,

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.470
if not straight into federal prison.

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:53.370
But there is one last wrinkle,

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.870
because the Secret Service are
not the only guys with guns

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:56.920
in the White House.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.220
What about the military?

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.980
Well, there's been lots
of speculation about

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.640
whether Donald Trump
could use the military

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.050
to keep himself in power.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.350
This isn't likely.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:05.850
The military follows a chain of command,

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.390
and when Joe Biden is sworn in,

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.410
he will be the commander in chief,

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.340
and President Trump loses all authority.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.440
If President Trump makes any kind of order

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.570
after noon on January 20th, 2021,

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.830
the military will not follow those orders.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.840
And it's also worth noting
that America has laws

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.500
mandating political neutrality
by members of the military.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.720
The military is not supposed
to dabble in domestic affairs.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.450
The Uniform Code of Military Justice,

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.040
or UCMJ, is the code of conduct applicable

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.390
to members of the armed forces,

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.780
and certain other individuals
closely associated

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.060
with the armed forces.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.810
The UCMJ sets forth procedures

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.740
for trials by courts martial,

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.540
and other disciplinary
actions to enforce these laws.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:45.740
Now, it's important to note
that the UCMJ does not apply

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.720
to the president.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.530
But Article 88 of the
UCMJ does make it a crime

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:51.947
for any officer in the
armed forces to, quote,

00:12:51.947 --> 00:12:54.277
"use contemptuous words against officials

00:12:54.277 --> 00:12:55.657
"of any branch of the US government,

00:12:55.657 --> 00:12:57.150
"or any state government."

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.340
The officer cannot make
any derogatory statements

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.150
against the US president,
and if a person does,

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:04.210
he or she could be court-martialed.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:05.630
Yes, this is an impingement

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.350
on the officer's First Amendment rights,

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.890
but it's something that
they knowingly give up

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.350
when they join the military.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.290
Article 88 is one of many
reasons you don't see

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.890
active duty military officers
critiquing Donald Trump.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.590
They are sworn to uphold
political neutrality.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:18.810
However, what if they're called upon

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.150
by a president to do something
that's arguably illegal,

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.950
or given orders by an ex-president?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:26.110
Well, the military is not supposed to obey

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.250
illegal unconstitutional orders.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.250
Obviously, we hope we
don't ever get to a point

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.390
where military officers have to decide

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:35.010
whether orders are illegal or not.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.730
It's up to the military
leadership to ensure

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:39.510
that all presidential orders are lawful.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:40.840
But if Joe Biden is president,

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.420
then he is the commander in chief.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.580
If President Trump tries
to order the military

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.980
to do anything, then
that is an illegal order.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.010
And when it comes to presidents gone wild,

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:52.170
we have one close
historical example to go by.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.890
When Nixon's time was
running out back in 1974,

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.440
many feared that he would
lean on his good friend,

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.210
who just happened to be the
commandant of the Marine Corps.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.450
Now, the story is that
Secretary of Defense

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.210
James Schlesinger was so
worried about Nixon issuing

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.940
illegal orders that he told
the Joint Chiefs of Staff

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:11.340
not to implement any direct
orders from President Nixon

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:13.960
that was not relayed through Schlesinger.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.380
Now, we don't know if this
story is historically accurate.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.660
Historians disagree about
what actually happened,

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:20.940
but it does show that
military leadership have given

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.260
lots of thought to what might happen

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.460
if a president started a meltdown.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.460
And in fact, Mark Milley,

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.220
the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff,

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.970
said that the military
would not be involved

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.200
in moderating or intervening any disputes.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.993
- We do not take an oath to an individual.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.430
No, we do not take an oath to a country,

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.810
a tribe, or religion.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.800
We take an oath to the Constitution.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.240
- In his view, it's
Congress' job to figure out

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:47.620
what's happening and prevent
it, not the military's.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.560
Milley is correct that
the Constitution is silent

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:50.640
on this exact scenario.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.550
However, he's probably
already thought about

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.140
what would happen if President Trump

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:55.620
wanted to remain in power.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.390
In August, two retired army
officers wrote an open letter

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:01.020
to Milley stating that
if Trump is holed up

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.200
in the White House with
armed supporters inside,

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:06.140
the military must defend
the rightful president,

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.367
stating, quote, "In the
constitutional crisis

00:15:08.367 --> 00:15:11.127
"described above, your duty
is to give unambiguous orders

00:15:11.127 --> 00:15:13.437
"directing US military forces to support

00:15:13.437 --> 00:15:15.517
"the constitutional transfer of power.

00:15:15.517 --> 00:15:16.587
"Should you remain silent,

00:15:16.587 --> 00:15:18.787
"you will be complicit in a coup d'etat.

00:15:18.787 --> 00:15:19.867
"You were rightly criticized

00:15:19.867 --> 00:15:21.267
"for your prior active complicity

00:15:21.267 --> 00:15:22.367
"in the president's use of force

00:15:22.367 --> 00:15:24.797
"against peaceful protestors
in Lafayette Square.

00:15:24.797 --> 00:15:27.137
"Your passive complicity
in an extralegal seizure

00:15:27.137 --> 00:15:30.070
"of political power would be far worse."

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.850
But whether it's the military
or the Secret Service,

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:35.840
on January 20th, Donald Trump
doesn't need to go home,

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.100
but he can't stay here.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.307
And as Joe Biden put it,

00:15:38.307 --> 00:15:40.377
"The United States government
is perfectly capable

00:15:40.377 --> 00:15:43.540
"of escorting trespassers
out of the White House."

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.950
But if President Trump does
stay past noon on January 20th,

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:50.010
he'll be trading his very
poorly tailored suits and ties

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.660
